#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105905 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105561 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3173d361-b91d-5699-97d8-6595ef59d0a3" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Area of a Quadrilateral"}] :question/id #uuid "b41b2354-c339-5398-ab43-5886b8447c1c" :question/math-academy-id "e-3294" :question/problem "Rounded to the nearest integer, what is the area of the quadrilateral $ABCD?$\n\n![](images/bc/bc9f32a9c0e8b042498a72e808a29274bd505e786d8ec43d0e0bc9888fdf6e44.png)" :question/worked-solution "The area of the quadrilateral $ABCD$ is the sum of the areas of the triangles $\\triangle ABC$ and $\\triangle ADC$ (see the illustration below).\n\n![](images/ac/acd2e923a65d0821cd59ed8b8274ceb5fc38def896467e37c8b1d454f958699e.png)\n\n First, we find the area for $\\triangle ABC,$ and get\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{ABC} & =\\frac{1}{2}(42)(35)\\operatorname{sin}⁡{36}^{∘} \\\\  & =735\\operatorname{sin}⁡{36}^{∘} \\\\  & ≈432.022\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to three decimal places.\n\nNow we find the area for $\\triangle ADC,$ and get\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{ADC} & =\\frac{1}{2}(20)(18)\\operatorname{sin}⁡{80}^{∘} \\\\  & =180\\operatorname{sin}⁡{80}^{∘} \\\\  & ≈177.265\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to three decimal places.\n\nFinally, we add together the areas of our two triangles to determine the area of $ABCD.$ We get\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{ABCD} & ={A}_{ABC}+{A}_{ADC} \\\\  & =432.022+177.265 \\\\  & ≈609\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsequently, to the nearest integer, the area of the quadrilateral $ABCD$ is $609.$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3173d361-b91d-5699-97d8-6595ef59d0a3" :knowledge-point/question-generator {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186556101 :question-generator/id #uuid "6893e50d-e3f7-5b49-8a0d-a1072f81fe87" :question-generator/script "generate/scratch/17592186105905.py"} :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186106087 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/