db/id #edb/ref 17592186104784} {:answer/id #uuid "f212af3d-14ce-5430-8e0d-ebf2c473beac" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "46.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186104785} {:answer/id #uuid "358fdfcf-9dc7-5768-b6ee-2fbdf0a6a7b4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "47.4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186104786} {:answer/id #uuid "5e7a3aa7-b0f9-5de4-b78a-8ca8b6f7052f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "42.3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186104787}] :answer-field/id #uuid "9e80d5c1-4641-5da9-a2bc-641c532e791f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186104782}] :question/id #uuid "419a42dc-188f-5378-85e0-27d5bb64db37" :question/math-academy-id "q-54258" :question/problem "![](images/cc/cc23cf5b5df6c51aac404c9e6a95ba3cfbdb2279bcd3dea11c6d56966d91a8dd.png)\n\nRounded to the nearest tenth, what is the area of the quadrilateral $ABCD$?\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question." :question/requires-calculator true} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186234325 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3173d361-b91d-5699-97d8-6595ef59d0a3" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Area of a Quadrilateral"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "02e1a207-f9d0-53f3-b9be-3206f74c6704" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "85" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512106} {:answer/id #uuid "992ff176-6fda-5a2c-8659-55baf90a83fa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "90" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512458} {:answer/id #uuid "af6bec52-f2b1-55fa-890f-584e44e51b59" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "61" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512510} {:answer/id #uuid "c3294de8-305e-5066-b9e4-7eebd339a6e5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "78" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512565} {:answer/id #uuid "ea211255-4798-55dc-866b-aae486ca03e7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512663}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "992ff176-6fda-5a2c-8659-55baf90a83fa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "90" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512458} :answer-field/id #uuid "a5f55799-fa35-55be-b5e7-23ed06c306d5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512814}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5a33798d-52c0-57f6-a233-6585edd299f2" :question/math-academy-id "q-72754" :question/problem "![](images/4c/4ce20d9d732816efda0a2fd3aebabc467f9f2c73d0b6037f4ad8f95d8e8ef1e7.png)\n\nRounded to the nearest integer, what is the area of the quadrilateral $ABCD?$" :question/worked-solution "The area of the quadrilateral $ABCD$ is the sum of the areas of the triangles $△ABD$ and $△BDC$ (see the illustration below).\n\n![](images/6e/6e070d26915bcb11118f5a23f36b80038d5dd865e32a8517a12c10939ca02f0b.png)\n\nFirst, we find the area of $△ABD:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{ABD} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 6\\cdot 8\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{85}^{∘} \\\\  & =24\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{85}^{∘} \\\\  & ≈23.908\\,7,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to four decimal places.\n\nNow we find the area of $△BCD:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{BCD} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 14\\cdot 16\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{36.4}^{∘} \\\\  & =112\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{36.4}^{∘} \\\\  & ≈66.462\\,9,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to four decimal places.\n\nFinally, we add together the areas of our two triangles to determine the area of $ABCD:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{ABCD} & ={A}_{ABD}+{A}_{BCD} \\\\  & ≈23.908\\,7+66.462\\,9 \\\\  & ≈90.371\\,6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsequently, to the nearest integer, the area of the quadrilateral $ABCD$ is $90.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186295111 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3173d361-b91d-5699-97d8-6595ef59d0a3" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Area of a Quadrilateral"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a6cee6b4-2a3f-5b80-8f79-bbdc774e729c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "52" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293590}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a6cee6b4-2a3f-5b80-8f79-bbdc774e729c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "52" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293590} :answer-field/id #uuid "e0a67366-7358-5ccd-9b0a-b78d1e7fee7b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294715}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1e17900e-d26f-58a6-baab-ca3dab29afb6" :question/math-academy-id "q-279762" :question/problem "![](images/54/54265327c77bedb300fe0d1f1f08ca3ab2d7ae37f35f49007d3f20ab3a21dbaa.png)\n\nRounded to the **nearest integer**, the area of the parallelogram $ABCD$ is{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "The diagonal $\\overset{―}{AC}$ divides the parallelogram into two congruent triangles. Therefore, the area of the parallelogram is twice the area of $△ACB$ (see the illustration below).\n\n![](images/b1/b1d0cf7c5a7c6ad7f0f52c8686239920fabcb05be57372ae0c7c9c9491838a52.png)\n\n Computing the area of $△ACB,$ we find\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{ACB} & =\\frac{1}{2}(10)(6)\\operatorname{sin}⁡{60}^{∘} \\\\  & =30\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{60}^{∘} \\\\  & ≈25.981,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to three decimal places. Consequently,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{ABCD} & =2{A}_{ACB} \\\\  & =2\\cdot 25.981 \\\\  & =51.962.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, to the **nearest integer**, the area of the parallelogram is $52.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297160 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3173d361-b91d-5699-97d8-6595ef59d0a3" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Area of a Quadrilateral"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "45026583-2f3c-517d-8eb5-a28f4404f1e5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "35.2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295658}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "45026583-2f3c-517d-8eb5-a28f4404f1e5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "35.2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295658} :answer-field/id #uuid "d0829f4e-98e2-572d-86bc-74f61d3d7503" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297067}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "3bb44f47-acad-5cce-bb2a-a2f32b8da827" :question/math-academy-id "q-285703" :question/problem "![](images/da/dafaf2421aaa9be80c472b4dde7c941defb94f7f3533fda4ebb2fdcee2b60e31.png)\n\nIn square units rounded to the **nearest tenth**, the area of the quadrilateral $ABCD$ is{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "The area of the quadrilateral $ABCD$ is the sum of the areas of the triangles $△ABD$ and $△BDC$ (see the illustration below).\n\n![](images/cd/cd9363a3cc686ae45f49c982f4b31ad75b7c7897dcf7e8af58e530dba6946e1d.png)\n\nFirst we find the area for $△ABD:$ \n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{ABD} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 6\\cdot 7\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{50}^{∘} \\\\  & =21\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{50}^{∘} \\\\  & ≈16.086\\,9,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to four decimal places.\n\nNow we find the area for $△BCD:$ \n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{BDC} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 7\\cdot 8\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{43}^{∘} \\\\  & =28\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{43}^{∘} \\\\  & ≈19.096\\,0,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to four decimal places.\n\nFinally, we add together the areas of our two triangles to determine the area of $ABCD:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{ABCD} & ={A}_{ABD}+{A}_{BDC} \\\\  & ≈16.086\\,9+19.096\\,0 \\\\  & ≈35.182\\,9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsequently, to the **nearest tenth**, the area of the quadrilateral $ABCD$ is $35.2.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297161 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3173d361-b91d-5699-97d8-6595ef59d0a3" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Area of a Quadrilateral"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6d4ed0c9-7f6f-5206-af74-9b5a71b8bb26" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "28" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295871}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6d4ed0c9-7f6f-5206-af74-9b5a71b8bb26" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "28" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295871} :answer-field/id #uuid "bfa377d1-aa1d-58ff-8f43-f26275cc3530" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297031}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8934630b-77d1-55ee-b8d1-51a8be5db47e" :question/math-academy-id "q-285737" :question/problem "![](images/48/48dec69962b09e9c189de23c398db63066b6da8d62a04f1cd01fdc9f333f899f.png)\n\nRounded to the **nearest integer**, the area of the parallelogram $ABCD$ is{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "The diagonal $\\overset{―}{AC}$ divides the parallelogram into two congruent triangles. Therefore, the area of the parallelogram is twice the area of $△ACB$ (see the illustration below).\n\n![](images/d6/d6a654d3154ba8af8fc4f7654e62c6bacfede7017322aeed21a143e2634dcd14.png)\n\n Computing the area of $△ACB,$ we find\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{ACB} & =\\frac{1}{2}(4)(8)\\operatorname{sin}⁡{120}^{∘} \\\\  & =16\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{120}^{∘} \\\\  & ≈13.856,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to three decimal places. Consequently,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{ABCD} & =2{A}_{ACB} \\\\  & =2\\cdot 13.856 \\\\  & =27.712.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, to the **nearest integer**, the area of the parallelogram is $28.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186332914 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3173d361-b91d-5699-97d8-6595ef59d0a3" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Area of a Quadrilateral"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0da74ef9-bc35-5bd4-a775-6227e3770b67" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "33" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330069} {:answer/id #uuid "4cab3170-0757-5382-a642-6a610aa18961" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "40" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330646} {:answer/id #uuid "51dae920-7e93-5d91-8ef7-09f5119e363c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "38" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330692} {:answer/id #uuid "af914ae5-dadd-5a35-bda2-56290cd884a3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "42" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331501} {:answer/id #uuid "e18ffbce-0f6c-59ce-84c9-1967feb16d19" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "30" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331944}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0da74ef9-bc35-5bd4-a775-6227e3770b67" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "33" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330069} :answer-field/id #uuid "489b8504-24f4-5803-ae22-0dec31049edf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332322}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "9a963f45-1ffb-5d74-b38f-c635a0c24c20" :question/math-academy-id "q-54339" :question/problem "![](images/f1/f1ae263b71fa17fd648464c24b307c064c9e657c2c9f6b36faf8c9819f1fb285.png)\n\nFind, to the nearest integer, the area of the parallelogram $ABCD.$" :question/worked-solution "The diagonal $\\overset{―}{AC}$ divides the parallelogram into two congruent triangles. Therefore, the area of the parallelogram is twice the area of $△ACD$ (see the illustration below).\n\n![](images/a6/a60b049aef53aef28802b084b3e445fd6253978500ca981d3b799977523cdd71.png)\n\n Computing the area of $△ACD,$ we find\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{ACD} & =\\frac{1}{2}(8)(5)\\operatorname{sin}⁡{55}^{∘} \\\\  & =20\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{55}^{∘} \\\\  & ≈16.383,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to three decimal places. Consequently,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{ABCD} & =2{A}_{ACD} \\\\  & =2\\cdot 16.383 \\\\  & =32.766.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, to the nearest integer, the area of the parallelogram is $33.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186335939 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3173d361-b91d-5699-97d8-6595ef59d0a3" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Area of a Quadrilateral"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "03142fcd-6f19-5692-a3da-da502772ac2c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "83.4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333014} {:answer/id #uuid "0430ddd0-499d-53c2-994f-613bdc887648" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "88.2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333022} {:answer/id #uuid "454df806-b05f-5668-bfc1-d7cfdc549af7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "73.3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333630} {:answer/id #uuid "a5074c1a-1d5f-5090-b302-4eafa6e852a3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "76.6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334436} {:answer/id #uuid "d012d020-5f8d-544e-8a7f-5e3267236519" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "69.8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334803}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "454df806-b05f-5668-bfc1-d7cfdc549af7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "73.3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333630} :answer-field/id #uuid "fe2925de-ca80-5513-860d-a4f360e0060a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335683}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "bbe5d0e1-3ef1-5eeb-b6da-bb45b64850c9" :question/math-academy-id "q-67787" :question/problem "![](images/48/488389632139d269e24958275ee20a9e5f8582fd0966e4d935487d238a463180.png)\n\nRounded to the nearest tenth, what is the area of the quadrilateral $ABCD?$" :question/worked-solution "The area of the quadrilateral $ABCD$ is the sum of the areas of the triangles $△ABD$ and $△BDC$ (see the illustration below).\n\n![](images/68/68f5708d49577befe9bac6a7aaf6a54fcdb30dcd344367d2c69b8924093dbb61.png)\n\n \n\nFirst we find the area for $△ABD:$ \n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{ABD} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 12\\cdot 14\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{42.1}^{∘} \\\\  & =84\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{42.1}^{∘} \\\\  & ≈56.315\\,8,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to four decimal places.\n\nNow we find the area for $△BCD:$ \n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{BDC} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 5\\cdot 7\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{103.8}^{∘} \\\\  & =17.5\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{103.8}^{∘} \\\\  & ≈16.994\\,8,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to four decimal places.\n\nFinally, we add together the areas of our two triangles to determine the area of $ABCD:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{ABCD} & ={A}_{ABD}+{A}_{BDC} \\\\  & =56.315\\,8+16.994\\,8 \\\\  & =73.310\\,6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsequently, to the nearest tenth, the area of the quadrilateral $ABCD$ is $73.3.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186335940 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3173d361-b91d-5699-97d8-6595ef59d0a3" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Area of a Quadrilateral"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "018db6be-c2e0-5b71-a965-9b8b09b6b735" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "416" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333001} {:answer/id #uuid "0d660a41-028d-58ab-aa41-4492c238acc7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "462" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333106} {:answer/id #uuid "30e73ae1-8ede-5d25-9355-5c9e2abec14c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "458" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333440} {:answer/id #uuid "b829245a-508c-5df4-ab92-1586e59a733f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "437" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334602} {:answer/id #uuid "ec58f96d-7f07-5f65-a5c3-6ba3c108fcad" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "422" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335058}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "30e73ae1-8ede-5d25-9355-5c9e2abec14c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "458" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333440} :answer-field/id #uuid "4fd4a639-ac17-50f3-9f71-1f9152848f0e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335392}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "dd32da9e-3e34-5cd6-ac25-c9a996a26523" :question/math-academy-id "q-67788" :question/problem "![](images/b0/b0b100942a658966a5feea8a8677e7cfe86f21970a443385ff06034bbcb3d497.png)\n\nRounded to the nearest integer, what is the area of the quadrilateral $ABCD?$" :question/requires-calculator true :question/worked-solution "The area of the quadrilateral $ABCD$ is the sum of the areas of the triangles $△ACD$ and $△ABC$ (see the illustration below).\n\n![](images/7e/7e3232258a523e4dbfebb6c380f5b88c2a54036b4d719e70ebf9060054f825d7.png)\n\n \n\nFirst we find the area for $△ACD:$ \n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{ACD} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 18\\cdot 21\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{60}^{∘} \\\\  & =189\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{60}^{∘} \\\\  & ≈163.679,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $3$ decimal places.\n\nNow we find the area for $△ABC:$ \n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{ABC} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 36\\cdot 30\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{33}^{∘} \\\\  & =540\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{33}^{∘} \\\\  & ≈294.105,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $3$ decimal places.\n\nFinally, we add together the areas of our two triangles to determine the area of $ABCD:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{ABCD} & ={A}_{ACD}+{A}_{ABC} \\\\  & =163.679+294.105 \\\\  & =457.784\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsequently, to the nearest integer, the area of the quadrilateral $ABCD$ is $458.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186341859 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3173d361-b91d-5699-97d8-6595ef59d0a3" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Area of a Quadrilateral"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4d011d15-855e-593b-a305-503c6f4d7b4a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "65" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339829} {:answer/id #uuid "5049855a-0cf1-52ff-a6d7-82ad580a1998" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "135" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339858} {:answer/id #uuid "65970e9b-6b55-55f9-87cb-642a2bfcf59a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "132" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340026} {:answer/id #uuid "810e57dc-6211-51e2-9530-7c30c274a5a4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "98" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340286} {:answer/id #uuid "941f7586-f901-520c-ba5a-d3f77fa4895c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "112" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340460}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5049855a-0cf1-52ff-a6d7-82ad580a1998" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "135" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339858} :answer-field/id #uuid "59a7e60a-6a2a-50ed-b8ee-1ebc1c309e07" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341540}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c1e965d5-3d0b-5c28-9671-3eb1e1598d0f" :question/math-academy-id "q-72768" :question/problem "![](images/36/36af7324fd2112d94feddc5a1a02a91d97bbc0866cb93a6ca711dd73f566305a.png)\n\nFind, to the nearest integer, the area of the parallelogram $ABCD.$" :question/worked-solution "The diagonal $\\overset{―}{AC}$ divides the parallelogram into two congruent triangles. Therefore, the area of the parallelogram is twice the area of $△ACB$ (see the illustration below).\n\n![](images/7c/7cfcb5cdf77b4afbf25afd64e37bb33f0ab2c211e09659181bfc16db0ccd2db7.png)\n\n Computing the area of $△ACB,$ we find\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{ACD} & =\\frac{1}{2}(18)(8)\\operatorname{sin}⁡{70}^{∘} \\\\  & =72\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{70}^{∘} \\\\  & ≈67.658,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to three decimal places. Consequently,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{ABCD} & =2{A}_{ACB} \\\\  & =2\\cdot 67.658 \\\\  & =135.316.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, to the nearest integer, the area of the parallelogram is $135.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186547012 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3173d361-b91d-5699-97d8-6595ef59d0a3" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Area of a Quadrilateral"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "62ee6c7b-5ed0-5fbc-bb1a-2eb180c50a25" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "41" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546468} {:answer/id #uuid "761357af-b1cf-58ba-aa81-8798f7d22c51" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "45" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546514} {:answer/id #uuid "adee8728-bdb1-56dd-815f-113cd38c7423" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "39" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546640} {:answer/id #uuid "e75bdd06-64ae-503e-b1d5-c6851246b93d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "37" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546768} {:answer/id #uuid "f14b0185-0e87-545d-8523-8be2d0e389d7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "35" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546793}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e75bdd06-64ae-503e-b1d5-c6851246b93d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "37" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546768} :answer-field/id #uuid "3c4e9d14-c6c0-59b2-ad73-b4792a7449af" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546852}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "66cc8550-5653-59d7-83fc-1ba0962c771f" :question/math-academy-id "q-54340" :question/problem "![](images/87/873c7f6b6e036f592f693bf2d20e1980b890f888d08af40b775cb77deba07a76.png)\n\nRounded to the nearest integer, what is the area of the parallelogram $ABCD?$" :question/worked-solution "The diagonal $\\overset{―}{BD}$ divides the parallelogram into two congruent triangles. Therefore, the area of the parallelogram is twice the area of $△ABD$ (see the illustration).\n\n![](images/75/7572dac85d8e6029b52d199bdfcb87b4a92ffafc008fe999c10848153f9f67d8.png)\n\n Computing the area of $△ABD,$ we find\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{ABD} & =\\frac{1}{2}(10)(6)\\operatorname{sin}⁡{38}^{∘} \\\\  & =30\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{38}^{∘} \\\\  & ≈18.470,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to three decimal places. Consequently,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{ABCD} & =2{A}_{ABD} \\\\  & =2\\cdot 18.470 \\\\  & =36.940.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, to the nearest integer, the area of the parallelogram is $37.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186547025 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3173d361-b91d-5699-97d8-6595ef59d0a3" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Area of a Quadrilateral"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "20078475-9fa7-56a0-a1a7-b2ef14a5f272" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "245" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546320} {:answer/id #uuid "2288c623-2025-50ca-9e29-2593b12d6fac" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "222" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546325} {:answer/id #uuid "c0de9861-7e04-5dd3-92eb-73257a63f700" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "205" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546684} {:answer/id #uuid "cdf1bd15-fb6d-58ed-a02e-de5eab09e256" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "192" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546708} {:answer/id #uuid "f4619caf-e3be-5779-a397-5eca1ee69630" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "230" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546801}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f4619caf-e3be-5779-a397-5eca1ee69630" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "230" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546801} :answer-field/id #uuid "71b130ba-6ae3-550e-b29f-ba671825e730" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546876}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "81669d7f-c6da-5c9d-8581-df25b358ada6" :question/math-academy-id "q-54338" :question/problem "![](images/24/243e5fd1911db6fc7dc940a16082c7369c63f913d78d9e18324d977540a310cb.png)\n\nFind, to the nearest integer, the area of the parallelogram $ABCD.$" :question/worked-solution "The diagonal $\\overset{―}{BD}$ divides the parallelogram into two congruent triangles. Therefore, the area of the parallelogram is twice the area of $△CBD$ (see the illustration below).\n\n![](images/da/da5c25d9e1e54a79b8e2c8532d4571dd42ccd4e6e6a3fa69aa1fc9075c19b39d.png)\n\n Computing the area of $△CBD,$ we find\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{CBD} & =\\frac{1}{2}(21)(12)\\operatorname{sin}⁡{66}^{∘} \\\\  & =126\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{66}^{∘} \\\\  & ≈115.107,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to three decimal places. Consequently,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{ABCD} & =2{A}_{CBD} \\\\  & =2\\cdot 115.107 \\\\  & =230.214.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, to the nearest integer, the area of the parallelogram is $230.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186556057 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3173d361-b91d-5699-97d8-6595ef59d0a3" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Area of a Quadrilateral"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "091b27af-d7a1-515d-b104-eaa4d333ff68" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "25.9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556053} {:answer/id #uuid "112123cb-757e-592c-bcc5-657d79933f62" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "194.2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556054} {:answer/id #uuid "4cf8c86f-5b8f-5088-b5b1-7fd64f54be93" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "362.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556064} {:answer/id #uuid "e44db984-9187-5181-80fa-c663461bafab" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "168.3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556095} {:answer/id #uuid "fd3f1256-bf92-5f25-bf62-8b729543bd57" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "725.0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556100}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4cf8c86f-5b8f-5088-b5b1-7fd64f54be93" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "362.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556064} :answer-field/id #uuid "83ccab36-87a8-545e-a1f1-0e48f5eaae48" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556071}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "1fbc0c8f-18ed-5226-a1e4-557184738889" :question/problem "![](images/b9/b9343557caba8d0816ce08f755e124d1648780523145cd6864d3718550432014.png)\n\nRounded to the nearest tenth, what is the area of the quadrilateral $ABCD$?\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question.\n\nThe diagram is not drawn to scale. Use the marked measurements. The marked angles are rounded to the precision shown; calculate the area estimate using the marked values." :question/worked-solution "The area of the quadrilateral $ABCD$ is the sum of the areas of the triangles $△ABD$ and $△BDC$ (see the illustration below).\n\n![](images/59/59dd651e6e27665841463b1d6f8f8409801ca6bd5f15428e2cb5cf65328a2528.png)\n\nFirst we find the area for $△ABD:$ \n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{ABD} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 21.1\\cdot 22.1\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{56.4}^{∘} \\\\  & =233.155\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{56.4}^{∘} \\\\  & ≈194.199\\,8,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to four decimal places.\n\nNow we find the area for $△BCD:$ \n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{BDC} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 24.2\\cdot 16.7\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{56.4}^{∘} \\\\  & =202.07\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{56.4}^{∘} \\\\  & ≈168.308\\,4,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to four decimal places.\n\nFinally, we add together the areas of our two triangles to determine the area of $ABCD:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{ABCD} & ={A}_{ABD}+{A}_{BDC} \\\\  & ≈194.199\\,8+168.308\\,4 \\\\  & ≈362.508\\,2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsequently, to the nearest tenth, the area of the quadrilateral $ABCD$ is $362.5.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186556065 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3173d361-b91d-5699-97d8-6595ef59d0a3" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Area of a Quadrilateral"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5b48715f-d7f7-51ed-a8d7-39cfed0d2ccc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "138.7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556067}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5b48715f-d7f7-51ed-a8d7-39cfed0d2ccc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "138.7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556067} :answer-field/id #uuid "717c1752-4a87-5be3-88ae-66ccafef2bf5" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556069}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "52a9fe04-6346-5a39-ab8f-c86dd541521a" :question/problem "![](images/13/131fbdc1d3e47edd13257d415ee888c2148ccb3716bfd97ddaaa16efaa56db15.png)\n\nIn square units rounded to the **nearest tenth**, the area of the quadrilateral $ABCD$ is{{field-1}}.\n\nEnter the rounded number using digits and a decimal point if needed.\n\nThe diagram is not drawn to scale. Use the marked measurements. The marked angles are rounded to the precision shown; calculate the area estimate using the marked values." :question/worked-solution "The area of the quadrilateral $ABCD$ is the sum of the areas of the triangles $△ABD$ and $△BDC$ (see the illustration below).\n\n![](images/1f/1f848c8c4766a074b4c2b8e7ecc1e71d23e9c2c1c89158b8988ab36b53879f61.png)\n\nFirst we find the area for $△ABD:$ \n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{ABD} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 13.6\\cdot 10\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{87.3}^{∘} \\\\  & =68\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{87.3}^{∘} \\\\  & ≈67.924\\,5,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to four decimal places.\n\nNow we find the area for $△BCD:$ \n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{BDC} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 8.7\\cdot 19.9\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{54.8}^{∘} \\\\  & =86.565\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{54.8}^{∘} \\\\  & ≈70.736\\,1,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to four decimal places.\n\nFinally, we add together the areas of our two triangles to determine the area of $ABCD:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{ABCD} & ={A}_{ABD}+{A}_{BDC} \\\\  & ≈67.924\\,5+70.736\\,1 \\\\  & ≈138.660\\,6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsequently, to the **nearest tenth**, the area of the quadrilateral $ABCD$ is $138.7.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186556068 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3173d361-b91d-5699-97d8-6595ef59d0a3" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Area of a Quadrilateral"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b08d1199-8bf8-5b81-ba95-b6c22cf8c126" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "88" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556080}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b08d1199-8bf8-5b81-ba95-b6c22cf8c126" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "88" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556080} :answer-field/id #uuid "14440efa-6234-5e89-bd76-a3d48338cde5" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556055}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "70e4dbc4-d39e-56c5-b732-6b1f3dd60ee8" :question/problem "![](images/44/44c617ba56886e7efe82d2b5624cb65effb54978ba810623990860d154830c40.png)\n\nRounded to the **nearest integer**, the area of the parallelogram $ABCD$ is{{field-1}}.\n\nEnter the rounded number using digits and a decimal point if needed.\n\nThe diagram is not drawn to scale. Use the marked measurements. The dashed diagonal divides the parallelogram into two congruent triangles." :question/worked-solution "The diagonal $\\overset{―}{AC}$ divides the parallelogram into two congruent triangles. Therefore, the area of the parallelogram is twice the area of $△ACB$ (see the illustration below).\n\n![](images/44/44c617ba56886e7efe82d2b5624cb65effb54978ba810623990860d154830c40.png)\n\n Computing the area of $△ACB,$ we find\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{ACB} & =\\frac{1}{2}(6)(17)\\operatorname{sin}⁡{60}^{∘} \\\\  & =51\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{60}^{∘} \\\\  & ≈44.167,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to three decimal places. Consequently,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{ABCD} & =2{A}_{ACB} \\\\  & =2\\cdot 44.167 \\\\  & ≈88.334.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, to the **nearest integer**, the area of the parallelogram is $88.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186556073 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3173d361-b91d-5699-97d8-6595ef59d0a3" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Area of a Quadrilateral"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0087ce35-633e-5bb1-91c6-dc5054cd9772" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "73.4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556051} {:answer/id #uuid "224d4162-73d4-507d-9dff-d0df11cad464" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15.0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556058} {:answer/id #uuid "582f4049-209c-5697-8586-2c2c755df426" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "263.6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556066} {:answer/id #uuid "9bf55c7a-7253-58e2-833b-d58e701c73f0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "58.4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556075} {:answer/id #uuid "df930634-6d70-5c54-97d3-326e30505e72" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "131.8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556092}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "df930634-6d70-5c54-97d3-326e30505e72" :answer/type {:db/ident :