int/id #uuid "3173d361-b91d-5699-97d8-6595ef59d0a3" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Area of a Quadrilateral"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a9e435db-0327-5a0d-89dd-6b6919442bba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "94" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556078} {:answer/id #uuid "c7b5bed8-0df4-5779-a211-92c3cffb329c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "432" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556088} {:answer/id #uuid "c9707b78-0a7a-5dc5-a497-e949b9c08daa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "216" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556089} {:answer/id #uuid "df9eb1e0-6448-5054-97e0-b35a5285f814" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "187" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556093} {:answer/id #uuid "fbdcecd0-ef54-5a3f-9109-c956203b15a2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "108" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556098}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "df9eb1e0-6448-5054-97e0-b35a5285f814" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "187" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556093} :answer-field/id #uuid "240fe116-c60b-585d-bc29-6fabb08ceefe" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556059}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a758c7b9-2fca-5f7b-9e41-1dd87720b0f0" :question/problem "![](images/67/67555c7ecb4ca726c4153c7b4e6bcd377f06534bb42cbdc5b696b697788847c4.png)\n\nFind, to the nearest integer, the area of the parallelogram $ABCD.$\n\nThe diagram is not drawn to scale. Use the marked measurements. The dashed diagonal divides the parallelogram into two congruent triangles." :question/worked-solution "The diagonal $\\overset{―}{AC}$ divides the parallelogram into two congruent triangles. Therefore, the area of the parallelogram is twice the area of $△ACB$ (see the illustration below).\n\n![](images/67/67555c7ecb4ca726c4153c7b4e6bcd377f06534bb42cbdc5b696b697788847c4.png)\n\n Computing the area of $△ACB,$ we find\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{ACB} & =\\frac{1}{2}(18)(12)\\operatorname{sin}⁡{60}^{∘} \\\\  & =108\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{60}^{∘} \\\\  & ≈93.531,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to three decimal places. Consequently,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{ABCD} & =2{A}_{ACB} \\\\  & =2\\cdot 93.531 \\\\  & ≈187.062.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, to the nearest integer, the area of the parallelogram is $187.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186556082 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3173d361-b91d-5699-97d8-6595ef59d0a3" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Area of a Quadrilateral"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "79fffb65-226b-594a-aa22-0f4f4c72a6ec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "126" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556070} {:answer/id #uuid "b8d31c81-37cf-5e25-848b-3d24a03c8aa0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "55" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556084} {:answer/id #uuid "cdae530d-6cfa-5bc1-93ab-c4f4e2375cc8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "252" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556090} {:answer/id #uuid "db6cc186-fe5e-57ed-a442-5decdd9bc1e1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "63" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556091} {:answer/id #uuid "f7bcab47-0599-5d40-8019-94f89f8a64c9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "109" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556096}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f7bcab47-0599-5d40-8019-94f89f8a64c9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "109" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556096} :answer-field/id #uuid "04b78953-d30d-5275-98b5-d8ee62cdd70f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556052}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b40fc366-4e09-5d72-87e3-127966410a40" :question/problem "![](images/58/589b9b43c038ffb4a4dafac8e8f42f936478230f3721e4386a4c0a061e62103b.png)\n\nFind, to the nearest integer, the area of the parallelogram $ABCD.$\n\nThe diagram is not drawn to scale. Use the marked measurements. The dashed diagonal divides the parallelogram into two congruent triangles." :question/worked-solution "The diagonal $\\overset{―}{AC}$ divides the parallelogram into two congruent triangles. Therefore, the area of the parallelogram is twice the area of $△ACB$ (see the illustration below).\n\n![](images/58/589b9b43c038ffb4a4dafac8e8f42f936478230f3721e4386a4c0a061e62103b.png)\n\n Computing the area of $△ACB,$ we find\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{ACB} & =\\frac{1}{2}(14)(9)\\operatorname{sin}⁡{60}^{∘} \\\\  & =63\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{60}^{∘} \\\\  & ≈54.560,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to three decimal places. Consequently,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{ABCD} & =2{A}_{ACB} \\\\  & =2\\cdot 54.560 \\\\  & ≈109.120.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, to the nearest integer, the area of the parallelogram is $109.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186556083 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3173d361-b91d-5699-97d8-6595ef59d0a3" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Area of a Quadrilateral"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "28e03df9-8d32-5e16-97e1-d60734a64ed1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "38" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556060} {:answer/id #uuid "31d66741-51d6-54eb-a142-66b65661bc90" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "65" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556061} {:answer/id #uuid "351a935e-7b5b-5e85-ab50-708f07e1c524" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "75" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556062} {:answer/id #uuid "b3f19eed-e3b8-5f37-8f59-f52cd689c97b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "32" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556081} {:answer/id #uuid "fc07f286-f460-598e-ab66-400dee68350b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "150" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556099}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "31d66741-51d6-54eb-a142-66b65661bc90" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "65" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556061} :answer-field/id #uuid "bfa7c8b4-08f6-5285-b332-9a95f5c67461" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556087}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b411e2c1-d7e9-5814-9062-370425b62fa8" :question/problem "![](images/38/3844c3042ed7433f478f732aada7bfc73faa3f07608bf25778d4d87dc0a14968.png)\n\nFind, to the nearest integer, the area of the parallelogram $ABCD.$\n\nThe diagram is not drawn to scale. Use the marked measurements. The dashed diagonal divides the parallelogram into two congruent triangles." :question/worked-solution "The diagonal $\\overset{―}{AC}$ divides the parallelogram into two congruent triangles. Therefore, the area of the parallelogram is twice the area of $△ACB$ (see the illustration below).\n\n![](images/38/3844c3042ed7433f478f732aada7bfc73faa3f07608bf25778d4d87dc0a14968.png)\n\n Computing the area of $△ACB,$ we find\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{ACB} & =\\frac{1}{2}(15)(5)\\operatorname{sin}⁡{60}^{∘} \\\\  & =37.5\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{60}^{∘} \\\\  & ≈32.476,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to three decimal places. Consequently,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{ABCD} & =2{A}_{ACB} \\\\  & =2\\cdot 32.476 \\\\  & ≈64.952.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, to the nearest integer, the area of the parallelogram is $65.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186556085 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3173d361-b91d-5699-97d8-6595ef59d0a3" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Area of a Quadrilateral"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3709483f-4d15-50f4-9763-74ba51bf85fb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "162" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556063}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3709483f-4d15-50f4-9763-74ba51bf85fb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "162" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556063} :answer-field/id #uuid "a2be22cc-d519-5b67-bc44-6b6554e4d067" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556076}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "bbc655be-2c25-5c4c-b0fb-845d3b2f8f24" :question/problem "![](images/24/245045911890f7cbd669087241954a3b100c6d15ec1bf511e4557d6e89c47db9.png)\n\nRounded to the **nearest integer**, the area of the parallelogram $ABCD$ is{{field-1}}.\n\nEnter the rounded number using digits and a decimal point if needed.\n\nThe diagram is not drawn to scale. Use the marked measurements. The dashed diagonal divides the parallelogram into two congruent triangles." :question/worked-solution "The diagonal $\\overset{―}{AC}$ divides the parallelogram into two congruent triangles. Therefore, the area of the parallelogram is twice the area of $△ACB$ (see the illustration below).\n\n![](images/24/245045911890f7cbd669087241954a3b100c6d15ec1bf511e4557d6e89c47db9.png)\n\n Computing the area of $△ACB,$ we find\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{ACB} & =\\frac{1}{2}(11)(17)\\operatorname{sin}⁡{60}^{∘} \\\\  & =93.5\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{60}^{∘} \\\\  & ≈80.973,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to three decimal places. Consequently,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{ABCD} & =2{A}_{ACB} \\\\  & =2\\cdot 80.973 \\\\  & ≈161.946.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, to the **nearest integer**, the area of the parallelogram is $162.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186556094 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3173d361-b91d-5699-97d8-6595ef59d0a3" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Area of a Quadrilateral"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9ac27400-1dfb-5d36-9cec-997cbda94fe7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "135.8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556074}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9ac27400-1dfb-5d36-9cec-997cbda94fe7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "135.8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556074} :answer-field/id #uuid "941236ee-de88-5001-b113-1f06dfd6e21c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556072}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "e0b03d8e-7815-590d-877d-b365e88392d9" :question/problem "![](images/a9/a941692b5253644845c4311baeb7d3e681a0c9091803440c5ecc0980494fbfc8.png)\n\nIn square units rounded to the **nearest tenth**, the area of the quadrilateral $ABCD$ is{{field-1}}.\n\nEnter the rounded number using digits and a decimal point if needed.\n\nThe diagram is not drawn to scale. Use the marked measurements. The marked angles are rounded to the precision shown; calculate the area estimate using the marked values." :question/worked-solution "The area of the quadrilateral $ABCD$ is the sum of the areas of the triangles $△ABD$ and $△BDC$ (see the illustration below).\n\n![](images/b4/b4b6aacce80889f8d867015f7f9c4400acba3d51fced00264062968c8295204a.png)\n\nFirst we find the area for $△ABD:$ \n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{ABD} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 9.5\\cdot 10.3\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{120.7}^{∘} \\\\  & =48.925\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{120.7}^{∘} \\\\  & ≈42.068\\,3,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to four decimal places.\n\nNow we find the area for $△BCD:$ \n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{BDC} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 13.4\\cdot 14.4\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{76.4}^{∘} \\\\  & =96.48\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{76.4}^{∘} \\\\  & ≈93.774\\,8,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to four decimal places.\n\nFinally, we add together the areas of our two triangles to determine the area of $ABCD:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{ABCD} & ={A}_{ABD}+{A}_{BDC} \\\\  & ≈42.068\\,3+93.774\\,8 \\\\  & ≈135.843\\,1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsequently, to the **nearest tenth**, the area of the quadrilateral $ABCD$ is $135.8.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186556097 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3173d361-b91d-5699-97d8-6595ef59d0a3" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Area of a Quadrilateral"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1c641eab-ed7e-5b56-aa85-a6d95edb6429" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "340.9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556056}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1c641eab-ed7e-5b56-aa85-a6d95edb6429" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "340.9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556056} :answer-field/id #uuid "bcfa3340-4566-58d3-8f9a-71cbe342dc62" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556086}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "fa65bbaf-475a-5c9e-a456-e1fba26eb1ce" :question/problem "![](images/5a/5a611645078047bb51f06d090a3be1b3628045067b106354fa62a167f7737c10.png)\n\nIn square units rounded to the **nearest tenth**, the area of the quadrilateral $ABCD$ is{{field-1}}.\n\nEnter the rounded number using digits and a decimal point if needed.\n\nThe diagram is not drawn to scale. Use the marked measurements. The marked angles are rounded to the precision shown; calculate the area estimate using the marked values." :question/worked-solution "The area of the quadrilateral $ABCD$ is the sum of the areas of the triangles $△ABD$ and $△BDC$ (see the illustration below).\n\n![](images/cc/ccae61d17dd53252c3c08c885d92c7cc7444f97a339feed8db2e7568883e54ce.png)\n\nFirst we find the area for $△ABD:$ \n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{ABD} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 19.3\\cdot 18.7\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{94.1}^{∘} \\\\  & =180.455\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{94.1}^{∘} \\\\  & ≈179.993\\,2,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to four decimal places.\n\nNow we find the area for $△BCD:$ \n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{BDC} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 11.6\\cdot 29.3\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{71.2}^{∘} \\\\  & =169.94\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{71.2}^{∘} \\\\  & ≈160.873\\,6,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to four decimal places.\n\nFinally, we add together the areas of our two triangles to determine the area of $ABCD:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{ABCD} & ={A}_{ABD}+{A}_{BDC} \\\\  & ≈179.993\\,2+160.873\\,6 \\\\  & ≈340.866\\,8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsequently, to the **nearest tenth**, the area of the quadrilateral $ABCD$ is $340.9.$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Area of a Quadrilateral"}]}
